**Analysis of Beresheet issuance bug**

Beresheet v2 was provisioned with a full set of testnet accounts, including a Frontier EVM pallet test account with a balance of:
console.log(util.u8aToBn(util.hexToU8a('0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff')));
// 3402823669209384634633746074317682114550
This balance can be seen in the EVM system at [https://beresheet.edgscan.com/accounts](https://beresheet.edgscan.com/accounts) and it accounts for the extra staking inflation that has gone to JelliedOwl and other validators. You can also verify this against node/cli/src/chain_spec.rs (look for a comment that reads "account used in frontier").
